<title>USA: Westpoint buys Britain's P.J. Flower &amp; Co..</title>
<headline>Westpoint buys Britain's P.J. Flower &amp; Co..</headline>
<dateline>WEST POINT, Ga.</dateline>
<text>
<p>WestPoint Stevens Inc., the giant bed linens and towels maker, said Monday it acquired P.J. Flower &amp; Co. Ltd, a British manufacturer of bath linens and home furnishings, for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The company said the acquisition was made by its recently formed British subsidiary, WestPoint Stevens (U.K.) Ltd.</p>
<p>P.J. Flowers, a privately held firm, has $20 million in annual sales, WestPoint said.</p>
<p>The acquisition of P.J. Flower will help launch Westpoint's European business, it said.</p>
